from pathlib import Path
from record_step import record, ROOT
steps={
19:('Maven Java server','Created a Java 21 single-module Spring Boot application, pinned Boot 3.5.7 and Spring AI 1.1.8, and resolved the maintained MCP SDK 0.18.3 transitively. Generated Maven wrapper 3.9.11. Configured web-application-type none, disabled banner, and directed Logback to System.err. Dependencies include JDBC, PostgreSQL, Flyway PostgreSQL support, JNA DPAPI, JUnit/Mockito, WireMock and Testcontainers. Download cache stays in .tools, ignored by source control.','pom.xml; mvnw.cmd; mvnw; .mvn; application.yml; logback-spring.xml'),
20:('PostgreSQL infrastructure','Created a project-specific Compose stack using PostgreSQL 16 Alpine. Bound host port 55432 only to 127.0.0.1 to avoid collision with a possible existing database. Generated a random ignored local DB credential without printing it. Started the container and observed Healthy status. Named volume preserves data between normal restarts; do not use compose down -v unless intentionally deleting it.','infra/compose.yaml; .local/db-password (secret, do not share); src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__core.sql'),
21:('Pure parsing and validation','Implemented raw video IDs, approved watch/shorts/embed/shortlink URLs, exact host checks, rejection of userinfo/ports/fragments and encoded path ambiguity, and duplicate v parameter rejection. Channel parser supports UC IDs and handles; ambiguous vanity URLs fail explicitly. Duration.parse returns only positive integral seconds. First test run found Set.of.contains(null) when URL had no scheme; fixed explicit null guard and reran seven domain tests successfully.','domain/Input.java; domain/DomainTest.java; .local/first-tests.log; .local/second-tests.log'),
22:('YouTube provider implementations','Defined the YouTubeProvider boundary and separate official HTTP and synthetic fixture adapters. The official adapter uses fixed HTTPS Google endpoints, bounded bodies/timeouts, explicit endpoint methods, batch hydration, safe typed errors and no redirects or automatic retries. Personal sampling reads one bounded page per collection and reports nextPageToken truncation. Fixtures include absent tags/language, too-long duration, unavailable IDs, unrelated content and prompt injection; none represent real user data.','provider/YouTubeProvider.java; provider/OfficialYouTubeProvider.java; provider/FixtureYouTubeProvider.java; resources/fixtures/videos.json'),
23:('Durable quota preflight','Created separate SEARCH_CALLS and GENERAL_UNITS counters keyed by Pacific quota date. Reservation transaction locks buckets in stable order and rolls back all changes if either budget is insufficient. Provider attempts consume reserved cost before sending the request. Close settles unused capacity. Crash-abandoned reservations remain conservatively held for that day. Tests cover zero-provider-call rejection, concurrent final-unit contention, accounting and DST date boundaries.','quota/QuotaService.java; DatabaseIT.java; SemanticsTest.java; V1__core.sql'),
24:('Local OAuth bootstrap','Implemented a separate CLI mode with unpredictable state, S256 PKCE, temporary 127.0.0.1 callback listener, duplicate query rejection, 180-second consent deadline and official browser consent. Refresh credentials are protected with Windows DPAPI CurrentUser outside the project. Required scope is youtube.force-ssl, appropriate to mandatory playlist writes. A quota-accounted channel identity read binds the profile before save. Auth status never returns tokens; logout revokes credentials and removes local drafts. No live login was performed because Google Cloud is not configured.','oauth/TokenVault.java; oauth/WindowsTokenVault.java; cli/AdminCli.java'),
25:('Metadata overview tool','Wired get_video_overview from typed MCP input through parser, full read reservation and provider. Output names source=video_metadata, includes canonical URL and explicitly disclaims transcript/watch evidence. Errors use a stable safe envelope and MCP isError. Resources have real registered handlers.','mcp/CuratorTools.java; mcp/KnowledgeResources.java; application/CuratorService.java'),
26:('FR-1 similar videos','Implemented bounded seed lookup, one candidate search and batch hydration after reserving two general units and one search call. Ranker uses shared corpus smoothed TF-IDF and weighted metadata features. Deduplicates IDs, excludes seed, handles missing evidence as zero, returns component scores and stable ID ties. This is metadata similarity, not YouTube ranking or pedagogical quality proof.','domain/Ranking.java; CuratorService.similar; CuratorTools.similar'),
27:('FR-2 similar channels','Resolved the supplied channel selector via official ID/handle lookup, searched candidates and hydrated them. Compared title/description vectors using cosine, excluded seed and sorted score then ID. Unsupported legacy vanity aliases explicitly fail rather than guessing a channel identity. No subscriber-count popularity feature is used.','Input.channel; CuratorService.channels; OfficialYouTubeProvider.channel/searchChannels'),
28:('FR-3 personal recommendations','Combined authorized likes, subscriptions and playlist video text with .45/.30/.25 source weights. All source collections have bounded sample sizes and reported truncation. Extracted top profile terms for one candidate search, excluded already-known video IDs and returned explained profile cosine scores. Empty signals return INSUFFICIENT_PROFILE. No implicit watch history or cross-account argument exists.','CuratorService.recommend; OfficialYouTubeProvider.personal; Models.PersonalData'),
29:('FR-4 honest analysis','Aggregated deduplicated liked/playlist video categories/channels, separate subscription channel counts, exact positive duration median and bins. Built trends only from subscription/playlist-item added timestamps. Period comparison uses half-open UTC dates and reports unavailable when a source has no temporal evidence. Liked video publication dates are never represented as engagement dates.','application/Analytics.java; SemanticsTest.analyticsNoInventedLikeHistory'),
30:('Natural-language parser','Implemented an anchored bounded grammar for Make/Create/Build a N-hour/minute LANGUAGE playlist on TOPIC, maximum N UNIT per video. Explicitly supports English/Hindi/Spanish/French mapping. Ambiguous, missing or conflicting requests return NEEDS_CLARIFICATION. The typed plan_playlist remains available to an existing conversational client. Parsed and typed values pass the same Constraints constructor.','domain/PlaylistSelector.java; DomainTest.textGrammarDoesNotGuessAmbiguousNumbers'),
31:('Deterministic playlist selection','Applied hard duration, declared audio-language, duplicate, total upper bound and item-count constraints before admitting items. Selection follows deterministic relevance/ID order and reports excluded reasons and remaining shortfall. Empty feasible set fails explicitly. A regression fixture documents that greedy relevance is not global fill optimization (20 minutes versus two 11-minute videos under 22 minutes). No unsupported performance improvement is claimed.','PlaylistSelector.select; docs/design-playlist-optimizer.md; DomainTest.selectorDeterministicAndDocumentsGreedyLimitation'),
32:('Exact draft approval and safe commit','Serialized immutable proposal fields in a stable record order and hashed stored bytes with SHA-256. Preview contains account, title/privacy, interpreted constraints, ordered videos, duration, expiry and policy. CLI requires a real Console and the full fingerprint phrase; no MCP approval function exists. The DB checks account/digest/expiry and atomically consumes one grant. Commit journals each intention/result, persists remote IDs, reads back exact order, replays CREATED without writes, and stops ambiguous/partial retries for review. Tests target concurrency, altered proposal, expiry and unapproved writes.','persistence/DraftStore.java; cli/AdminCli.java; CuratorService.commit; DatabaseIT.java'),
33:('Full MCP surface','Registered ten typed MCP tools and five public knowledge resources plus a safe workflow prompt. Tool results include schemaVersion/requestId/asOf/fixture status; domain errors use isError and safe messages. No user-selectable token/account, arbitrary shell/SQL/URL or approval tool is exposed. CLI startup disables MCP server so human stdout cannot corrupt protocol mode.','mcp/CuratorTools.java; mcp/KnowledgeResources.java; McpServerApplication.java'),
34:('Product skill','Created video-to-playlist with metadata overview, similarity, constraints, exact preview, human local approval, guarded commit and truthful short analysis. Stop conditions include absent evidence, expiry, quota/auth failure and injection. Fixtures are never reported as live playlists; skill files do not imply automatic discovery in every client.',' .agents/skills/video-to-playlist/SKILL.md; evals/video-to-playlist/cases.json'),
35:('Common skills','Created brain-ingest, brain-refine, brain-query and local-check with actual workflow steps, distilled-note citations, failure conditions and separate evaluation scenarios. Applied ingest/refine/query to the project notes and recorded actions. The local-check command and protocol harness are being completed; their success will be reported only after execution.',' .agents/skills; brain/log.md; docs/brain-query-evidence.md; evals'),
36:('Unit and provider test suite','Added JUnit cases for parsers, hard constraints, deterministic scores, text ambiguity, PKCE known vector/state, Pacific dates and temporal semantics. WireMock tests exercise actual HTTP mapping, missing metadata, unavailable video, malformed JSON, exact endpoint/body and quota/auth/channel/rate errors without live access. Mockito reservation doubles verify charges at the boundary.','src/test/java; target/surefire-reports'),
37:('Database integration tests','Added Testcontainers PostgreSQL tests that migrate an empty real database, persist/reload proposals, reject owner/digest/expiry mismatches, run atomic quota/commit contention and test replay/account deletion. Containers are disposable and distinct from the persistent developer Compose database. No H2 substitute or silent Docker skip is configured.','DatabaseIT.java; target/failsafe-reports')}
